  "notes": [
    "Edges describe SDK production dependencies. Third-party dependencies, dev-only consumers, platform features and wire transports require separate implementation review.",
    "Invocation uses the core SchemaEvaluator seam; applications inject a concrete evaluator. There is no edge from invocation to the default evaluator.",
    "roles.checking is a shared policy classification, not an additional runtime package; each role owns its own admission and result checks.",
    "Rust role Wasm compilation is separately required. The existing TypeScript bridge does not thereby expose role APIs.",
    "One qualification concept spans the evaluator kit and repository-level tooling; it does not imply a universal runtime testing framework.",
    "Providers and external qualification fixtures use comparison for reuse identity. The production source-pull checker cannot certify the unavailable offered schema and has no comparison dependency.",
    "Default evaluation uses one original-node semantic Plan. Fixed document/meta/format checks and immutable pattern compilation remain distinct private mechanisms; the outgoing projection compiler is deleted."
  ],
